  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mover><munder><msub><mi>CaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Anhydrous</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>(b) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mover><mi>MgO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The dehydration of hydrated chloride of calcium can be achieved. The corresponding hydrated chloride of magnesium on heating suffer hydrolysis.</p><p>(c) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Amphoteric</p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ef5358c7-009b-448c-82b7-01b8e2487d1d-image.png\" style=\"width: 213px; height: 78px;\" /></p>",
